domain SemanticAuthoringDesignRevision3SelfCheck:
  description "Check design candidate v1 revision three against accepted ADR0032 without accepting it."
problem P1:
  |
    Determine whether revision three removes the identified time-boundary inconsistency
    while preserving unaffected accepted design contracts.
evidence E1:
  |
    The authoritative design candidate SHA256 is
    49181675114f6ced237ced68a335aa1e1edbb0eaa788379f0d6c09dc36a3e6f1.
    It identifies revision three and accepted ADR0032 as its current architectural
    authority.
evidence E2:
  |
    Section 7 no longer declares a whole-attempt elapsed maximum or a provider timeout
    literal. It excludes time from cumulative attempt budgeting and retains the call,
    step, token, byte, cost, progress-history, and recovery-strategy maxima.
evidence E3:
  |
    Sections 3.1 and 7 bind separate provider transport and worker execution policy
    identities. Provider timeout is a typed transport outcome; worker lease expiry is a
    recoverable technical outcome; neither is semantic failure or a whole-attempt
    semantic deadline.
evidence E4:
  |
    Provider timeout recovery is bounded to zero or one by a frozen route policy and
    remains unavailable until its exact value and time values satisfy ADR0032 evidence
    and owner-acceptance conditions. All recovery retains monotonic resource accounting
    and current fencing.
evidence E5:
  |
    The full Japanese projection SHA256 is
    31274ece3bc4b4540f5369941ad24ce0756854077d6b8b0d4b1e011d290e60d5
    and carries the same revision, contracts, pending values, and authority boundary.
evidence E6:
  |
    Current non-normative runtime WIP still contains maxAttemptElapsedMs 240000,
    maxProviderCallElapsedMs 60000, attempt elapsed admission, and whole-attempt
    termination. The design explicitly excludes implementation and activation.
premise C1:
  |
    A self-check can establish internal traceability but cannot substitute for the fresh
    independent review and exact owner acceptance required by the design lifecycle.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4:
  |
    Revision three corrects the four time-policy inconsistencies identified by the
    ADR0032 consistency check without weakening the retained non-time controls.
decision D2 based_on P1, E1, E5:
  |
    The English authority and complete Japanese review projection are aligned for the
    corrected scope.
decision D3 based_on P1, E6, C1:
  |
    Keep cc304 suspended. Runtime WIP is not yet conforming and must not be corrected or
    resumed until revision three receives fresh independent review and exact owner
    acceptance. This self-check is not that review or acceptance.
